A||||6||Fatal Error||Locker or tight limited slip.||||1||
Z||000000||Fatal Error||07-14-2001||08:45 PM||||Heya guys, I'm way new to the Fiero world (Don't even have one yet). I'm working on getting one.<P>I was wondering if there is any kind of a "locker" available or if fieros have posi-trac rear ends. <P>I'm curious about gearing as well. What is the stock gear ratio and what is a suggested replacement? <P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>'92 Chevy Silverado<BR>(wishing for 88GT Fiero)<BR>(working on 86GT Fiero)<BR>(Can afford 84 parts car)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Fatal Error (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||07-14-2001||08:51 PM||||Yeah, you know, I have the problem with terribly excessive wheel-spin all the time on my Fieros. I mean, the torque monster 2.8 that Fieros came with, what was GM smoking when they left out that limited slip.<P>(Now I'm being serious) Unless your putting something big in there, limited slip will only see use on dirt roads. Izusu I think makes one that will work, think its around 5K, its on thier site.<P>Gear ratios range in the Fiero depending on year, engine and tranny. FDs vary from 4.10 to 3.33 or similar. Chaning gears would reguire dis-assembly of transmission. Fieros do not use "rear-end" setup with drive-shaft, they use FWD tranny in back.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||07-14-2001||10:16 PM||||I don't know about lockers, but if you go here: <A HREF="http://www.mantapart.com/8794ber.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mantapart.com/8794ber.html</A>  and scroll down to the bottom you will find several limited slip diffs, performance gear sets and alternate FD ratios for both Isuzu 5-spds and Getrag 5-spds.<P>A parallel axis torque sensing LSD for Isuzu transmissions is available from <A HREF="http://www.isuzuperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.isuzuperformance.com</A>  or <A HREF="http://www.quaifeamerica.com" TARGET=_blank>www.quaifeamerica.com</A>   The diff is much cheaper from Quaife directly.<P>A crossed axis Torsen diff for the Getrag is available from the above mantapart address, but they only have one left and it is $1500.<P>The stock Getrag has a 3.61 FD, 3.50 1st gear, ~ 1.8 2nd, ~1.3 3rd, 0.98 4th, and 0.72 5th||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||07-14-2001||10:17 PM||||I will agree with Fiero56, unless you have big power on the way or do a lot of racing/AutoX, it's not worth it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jimmy||07-15-2001||01:24 PM||||Didn't GM offer a limited slip differential for a Getrag in one of their cars?  Was it an AchievaSCX?  If so I may begin a long and timeless journey to find one.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||07-15-2001||09:31 PM||||Yes, there was a "sub-option" of the W41 Achieva package which included a Torsen. Don't get your hopes up. You <I>won't</I> find one. They're that rare.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jimmy||07-16-2001||12:13 AM||||I know about the rairity from what others have said.  I do frequent yards quite a bit and just looking never hurt, besides its kinda fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I know of a few yards around here that get up to 10 cars a day on average.  I try and call/visit them once a week to see whats new.  <P>Is there a way to find out if the car has the torsen unit?  Is it listed on the car as a code?<P>Jim<P>87 GT<BR>87 GT T-TOP V8||||reg||1
